DevOps Interview Preparation AWS 
2–4 Years Experience | Tool 10 

Production-Level Cloud for DevOps Engineers

At 2–4 years, interviewers expect you to design, secure, monitor, and optimize AWS workloads, not just create resources.

🔹 Core AWS Interview Questions (2–4 yrs)

• Why AWS is widely used in production?
• AWS global infrastructure (Region, AZ, Edge)
• What happens when you launch an EC2 instance?
• EC2 vs ECS vs EKS — when to use which?
• EC2 vs ECS vs EKS — when to use which?
• AMI — why and how do you create it?
• Auto Scaling Groups — real use case
• Application Load Balancer vs Network Load Balancer
• How does ALB routing work?
• What is IAM and why is it critical?
• IAM user vs role vs policy
• How do you follow least-privilege access?
• How do you manage secrets in AWS?

🔹 Networking & Storage (Important for Interviews)

• What is VPC and why do we need it?
• Public vs private subnet
• Route tables and Internet Gateway
• NAT Gateway — why is it required?
• Security Group vs NACL
• S3 storage classes and lifecycle rules
• EBS vs EFS vs S3
• How do you secure S3 buckets?

🔹 DevOps-Focused AWS Services

• CloudWatch — metrics, logs, alarms
• CloudTrail — auditing & security
• AWS CodeBuild / CodeDeploy / CodePipeline
• ECR — Docker image registry
• Secrets Manager vs Parameter Store
• AWS CLI vs SDK
• How does AWS integrate with CI/CD?

🔹 Real-World AWS Scenarios

• EC2 instance is unreachable — troubleshooting steps
• Application is slow — how will you debug using AWS tools?
• Sudden AWS cost spike — how will you investigate?
• IAM permission issue blocking deployment — how to fix?
• How do you implement high availability in AWS?
• How do you do rollback in AWS deployments?

Interview Tip:
If you say:
 “We use ALB, Auto Scaling, IAM roles, and CloudWatch for production workloads”
you already sound like a strong 2–4 years DevOps engineer.
